### 1. Install Required Packages

```bash
npm install @azure/arm-resources @azure/identity
```

---

### 2. Import and Authenticate

```typescript
import { ResourceManagementClient } from "@azure/arm-resources";
import { DefaultAzureCredential } from "@azure/identity";

const subscriptionId = "your-subscription-id";
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const client = new ResourceManagementClient(credential, subscriptionId);
```
- `DefaultAzureCredential` automatically uses available credentials (local dev, environment, managed identity, etc.)【3:0†source】【3:2†source】.

---

### 3. Resource Group Operations

#### Create or Update Resource Group

```typescript
const groupName = "my-resource-group";
const params = { location: "eastus" };  // Additional properties can be added

const group = await client.resourceGroups.createOrUpdate(groupName, params);
console.log("Created/Updated Group:", group);
```

#### List All Resource Groups

```typescript
for await (const group of client.resourceGroups.list()) {
    console.log(group.name, group.location);
}
```

#### Get Specific Resource Group

```typescript
const group = await client.resourceGroups.get(groupName);
console.log("Fetched Group:", group);
```

#### Update Resource Group (PATCH)

```typescript
const updateParams = { tags: { project: "demo" } };
const updated = await client.resourceGroups.update(groupName, updateParams);
console.log("Updated Group:", updated);
```

#### Delete Resource Group (and wait for completion)

```typescript
await client.resourceGroups.beginDeleteAndWait(groupName);
console.log("Deleted Group:", groupName);
```
> This method waits until deletion is complete and is recommended for automated scripts【3:3†source】.

